{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"imperfect-crotchety-sponge","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Implement the adaptive byte/replay-cost snapshot cadence accepted by ADR 0118, default OFF globally. Preserve existing fixed-count behavior when compact.snapshot_alpha is unset or <= 0. Add config/env handling consistent with existing compact keys, pass pending-source and active-snapshot byte counts into the compaction trigger, preserve ADR 0035 fold horizon/retire/rebuild semantics, and add unit tests proving default behavior unchanged and positive alpha folds only when pending_source_bytes >= alpha * active_snapshot_bytes with the count floor retained.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- New config key compact.snapshot_alpha is default-off and documented in config ownership.\n- Mechanism-ratchet marker is present at the definition site: # mechanism-ok: config_key compact.snapshot_alpha — da70-18a5-898d-47ea\n- Tests cover default-off compatibility, alpha trigger behavior, first-snapshot/count-floor behavior, and no snapshot schema change.","id":"933f-e7d8-696a-4fbd","parent_id":"da70-18a5-898d-47ea","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Implement default-off compact.snapshot_alpha"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788911772035085001,"uuid":"5351cac2-3e35-4dd5-a506-18511f7094c9"}